+# Chat bots
+
+Any signed-in member can open **Set up chat bots** in `/account/edit`. `/bots`
+shows every active bot owned by that member; administrators can manage all bots.
+The shared new/edit form accepts a name and an optional avatar. Empty names are
+rejected server-side as well as by the browser.
+
+## Storage and delivery
+
+Startup adds `chat_bots(user_id, creator_id, code)` using the existing idempotent
+schema-additions mechanism. It does not alter Rails tables or migration versions.
+Each bot is an ordinary active member user, with no email address and an independent,
+random, unknowable password. User creation grants membership in all open rooms;
+ordinary room membership selectors include bots. The unique code has 32 random
+base58 characters. It is stored separately from user presentation data.
+
+Deleting a bot removes its credential and deactivates its user, retaining the name
+and avatar for historical messages. Credential and membership checks are repeated
+inside the message write transaction to serialize them against revocation.
+
+`POST /rooms/:room_id/:bot_code/messages` reads literal UTF-8 request bytes,
+regardless of Content-Type. Kit's RawBody marker disables both parameter parsing
+and method overrides for this endpoint alone. Whitespace-only input returns 422;
+invalid codes return 401, and missing or inaccessible rooms return 404. Successful
+posts return 201 with `Location: /messages/:id`.
+
+Text is HTML-escaped before entering Action Text; line breaks are retained. The
+normal Message::create callbacks handle search, unread memberships, and push jobs;
+the same broadcast_create helper used for human messages renders live updates.
+The endpoint accepts text only, not multipart attachment uploads, and uses kit's
+normal bounded raw-body size limit.
+
+## Credential handling
+
+- Management requires a normal session and CSRF checks. Every edit/update/delete
+  checks ownership or administrator status; other users get 404.
+- Bot pages have `Cache-Control: private, no-store`, disable Turbo snapshot caching,
+  and set `Referrer-Policy: no-referrer`. Codes only appear on the authorized index.
+- Bot models and list view models intentionally do not derive Debug.
+- The built-in access logger redacts the credential segment in bot API paths.
+- External reverse proxies, monitoring, shell history, and CI output also need to
+  redact these URLs. Use HTTPS and treat codes like passwords. Delete/recreate a
+  bot if its code is disclosed.
+
+## Per-member limit
+
+Administrators set **Bots per member** on `/account/edit`. Missing settings default to 5,
+including existing Rails accounts; the value lives in the existing account settings JSON.
+Only non-negative whole numbers are accepted. Zero disables creation for members.
+Administrators are exempt, regardless of how many bots they own or manage.
+
+The count includes only active bots owned by that member. Deletion frees a slot; lowering
+or reaching the limit never removes bots or prevents edits/deletions. The index hides
+**Add a chat bot** and shows **reached the limit** at or above the cap. `/bots/new` returns
+403 at the cap. `Bot::create` validates the current role, settings, and active count before
+creating a user in the same immediate write transaction, so direct POSTs, stale forms,
+concurrent requests, and other model callers cannot bypass the cap (validation returns 422).
+
+Run `docs/test-bot-limits.sh` for limit regressions, or `docs/test-bots.sh` for all full-stack
+bot regressions.
+
+## Verification
+
+- `docs/test-bots.sh`: creation/edit/deletion, avatar uploads, all-open-room joins,
+  private-room selection, owner/admin authorization, CSRF, over 100 bots without
+  pagination, raw-body edge cases/status codes, and live WebSocket author rendering.
+- `cargo test --workspace --exclude html5ever -- --test-threads=1`: passes (use a
+  higher file-descriptor limit, e.g. `ulimit -n 16384`, in constrained containers).
+- The installed Rust toolchain in the task environment lacks rustfmt and Clippy;
+  component installation was blocked by DNS, so those commands could not run.
